                            	  1700:     ; Submode 1.
                            	  1701:     ; Copies the whole play area to NT 0, one row each frame.
                            	  1702:     ;
                            	  1703:     ; TODO:
                            	  1704:     ; If mode 7 scrolls to a dark room, then it sets
                            	  1705:     ; CurRow to zero. Otherwise it would be $FF.
                            	  1706:     ; A positive value triggers this submode 1 to transfer
                            	  1707:     ; the whole play area.
                            	  1708:     ;
                            	  1709:     ; But why? As far as I can tell, the NT 0 is already in
                            	  1710:     ; a good state reflecting the new room. The only thing
                            	  1711:     ; needed is possibly to brighten the room by way of
                            	  1712:     ; changing the palette.
                            	  1713:     ;
                            	  1714:     ; So why does mode 7 trigger this?
                            	  1715:     ; Is there another mode that truly needs this behavior?
                            	  1716:     ;
02:0004110A 102C00E9        	  1717:     move.b  ($00E9,A4),D0
02:0004110E 6B06            	  1718:     bmi  _anon_z05_40
02:00041110 6100373A        	  1719:     jsr     CopyNextRowToTransferBuf
